   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 443 of the laws of 2006, amending the tax law relating\nto authorizing the town of Red Hook to impose a real estate transfer tax with\nrevenues therefrom to be deposited in said community preservation fund, in\nrelation to the effectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S9041",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9041-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §4, Chap 443 of 2006",
    "lawSection": "Taxation",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9041\n\nSPONSOR: HINCHEY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 443 of the laws of 2006, amending the tax law\nrelating to authorizing the town of Red Hook to impose a real estate\ntransfer tax with revenues therefrom to be deposited in said community\npreservation fund, in relation to the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo extend the town of Red Hook's preservation funds and tax on real\nestate transfers in the town until 2051.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends section 4 of chapter 443 of the laws of 2006, amending\ntax law relating to authorizing the town of Red Hook to impose a real\nestate transfer tax with revenues therefrom to be deposited in said\ncommunity preservation fund, so that the law shall expire December 31,\n2051.\n\nSection 2 states the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Town of Red Hook is requesting that the New York State Legislature\nintroduce and pass a bill to authorize the town to continue to impose a\nreal estate transfer tax for the period through December 26, 2051.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
